WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:07.120
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I am going&nbsp;
to explain a Japanese Romance Drama film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:15.920
called “My Tomorrow Your Yesterday.”&nbsp;
Spoilers ahead! Watch out and take care!
&nbsp;

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:25.280
It is the 15th of February. A 20 year old boy&nbsp;
named Takatoshi Minamiyama from Kyoto encounters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:32.160
a beautiful girl named Emi Fujuku on a train while&nbsp;
on his way to college. He is instantly smitten by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:38.000
her and he calls it love at first sight. Takatoshi&nbsp;
is a visual arts undergraduate student and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:44.400
political satirist. Tatakoshi is shy by nature and&nbsp;
initially suppresses his feelings but ultimately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:49.680
decides to approach her. He deliberately misses&nbsp;
his stop to talk to her. After getting off at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:54.640
her station, he awkwardly tells her that he has&nbsp;
fallen in love with her and asks for her email.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:02.400
When she tells him that she doesn’t have an email,&nbsp;
Takatoshi thinks she is turning him down and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:08.160
proceeds to leave but Emi stops him and assures&nbsp;
him that she really doesn’t use an email. The two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:13.520
then sit on a bench and get to know each other.&nbsp;
Emi reveals that she is a 20 years old cosmetology&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:18.640
student and she recently moved to the city.&nbsp;
When Emi asks him why he wanted to talk to her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:23.920
out of all the girls on the train, Takatoshi tells&nbsp;
her that he felt a sudden instinct to approach her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:29.040
which he can’t explain in words. He says that&nbsp;
he felt like he has known her for a long time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:34.560
Takatoshi proceeds to tell her something about&nbsp;
the Takaragaike lake but Emi suddenly gets up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:40.000
and tells him that she has to get going. Before&nbsp;
parting ways, Takatoshi asks Emi if they will meet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:46.000
again. This for some reason makes her emotional&nbsp;
and she says, “Until Tomorrow” before leaving. 
&nbsp;

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:51.040
At school, Takatoshi tells his best friend&nbsp;
Shoichi Ueyama, who is good with girls,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:57.040
about Emi. Ueyama finds it hard to believe that&nbsp;
a shy nerd like Takatoshi asked a girl for his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:02.160
phone number. Meanwhile, the latter is worried&nbsp;
if he will meet Emi again and Ueyama assures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:06.880
him that Emi will come looking for him.
The next day, Takatoshi looks for Emi on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:12.720
the train but doesn’t see her. Dejected, he goes&nbsp;
to the zoo to draw sketches for his assignment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:18.240
To his surprise, Emi approaches him at the zoo.&nbsp;
She compliments her drawing and comments that his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:23.600
school should definitely display his drawing.&nbsp;
However, Tatakoshi is puzzled thinking how Emi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:28.560
found him at the zoo. Emi tells him that he told&nbsp;
her his plans at the zoo in their last meeting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:34.400
and changes the topic. Tatakoshi is puzzled as&nbsp;
to when he said this but he is soon cut off by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:40.320
Emi. She asks him what he wanted to tell her about&nbsp;
the Takaragaike lake the last time and Takatoshi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:45.200
tells her that it is one of his favourite places.&nbsp;
He takes her there and reveals that he once fell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:51.120
off the pier and almost drowned in the lake when&nbsp;
he was saved by a woman. Emi reveals that she too&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:56.480
once almost died when she was five. This is a&nbsp;
strange coincidence that both of them share.
&nbsp;

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:01.840
This time, Emi gives Takatoshi her phone number&nbsp;
before parting ways. After returning home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:07.760
Tatakoshi tells Ueyama that he finally got Emi’s&nbsp;
number and Ueyama encourages him to ask her out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:13.840
on a date. Tatakoshi obligies and calls her but&nbsp;
doesn’t know how to ask her out. There, Ueyama&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:18.720
writes cards for him and helps him ask her out. 
The next day, Takatoshi learns that his school has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:23.040
displayed his drawing on the board. Following&nbsp;
the tips from his friend, Takatoshi goes to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:28.720
explore his dating spot by himself so he could&nbsp;
be as confident as possible before meeting Emi.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:34.000
Takatoshi then takes Emi to the same spot and&nbsp;
shows her an awesome time. He also takes her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:38.640
to a movie and the date goes really well.&nbsp;
At the end of the date, Takatoshi musters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:44.320
the courage to ask Emi to be his girlfriend.&nbsp;
Emi points out her flaws such as her emotions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:49.760
but Takatoshi tells her that he loves everything&nbsp;
about her. This too makes the girl tear up. 
&nbsp;

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:54.640
The next day, she shows up at Takatoshi’s house&nbsp;
to help him move to his new apartment, where she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.640 --> 00:04:00.560
finally meets his best friend Ueyama. After moving&nbsp;
the stuff in, Ueyama leaves but Emi stays with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:06.080
Takatoshi to help him organize his apartment.&nbsp;
She finds a mysterious box in one of the large&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:11.440
carton boxes and Takatoshi reveals that he met the&nbsp;
woman, who saved him from drowning at the lake,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:17.040
at a market 5 years ago and she gave him the box.&nbsp;
He also reveals that she asked him to not open&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:22.720
the box until they meet again. After arranging&nbsp;
his home, Takatoshi walks Emi to the station&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:27.440
and on the way, he musters up some courage&nbsp;
and nervously asks if he can hold her hand.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:32.960
She obliges and they hold each other’s hand for&nbsp;
the first time. Takatoshi is extremely happy as he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:38.080
is holding a girl’s hand for the first time while&nbsp;
Emi gets emotional and begins crying again. 
&nbsp;

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:42.240
Emi and Takatoshi start spending more and&nbsp;
more time with each other. Emi cooks for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:46.400
him and her cooking surprises him as her&nbsp;
food tastes just like his mother’s cooking.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:50.560
Emi speculates that maybe his mother&nbsp;
adds chocolate in her food just like her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:55.520
This surprises Takatoshi as he had never told&nbsp;
her that his mother adds chocolate in her dishes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:59.520
Takatoshi finds it strange that Emi is&nbsp;
able to predict things about his life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:03.840
as she had earlier predicted that his drawing&nbsp;
of a giraffe would be displayed at the school.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:08.400
However, Emi laughs it off and asks him what&nbsp;
he would do if she could predict the future.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:12.560
Takatoshi jokingly replies that he would&nbsp;
gamble all day and become filthy rich. 
&nbsp;

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:20.000
The two continue to spend more time together&nbsp;
and on the fifteenth day, the two make love&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:25.680
which again makes Emi emotional. It is getting&nbsp;
late again and Takatoshi walks Emi to the train&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:31.600
station. After returning home, Takatoshi finds&nbsp;
Emi’s journal on his table and goes through it. Lo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:37.360
and behold, the diary contains future predictions&nbsp;
of the next 15 days. The first entry is dated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:43.600
March 16 while the last entry is March 1. In an&nbsp;
entry from March 15, Emi has written that she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:49.280
met Takatoshoi’s parents. It seems Emi has written&nbsp;
them as if she is racing through time backwards.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:54.400
Takatoshi then receives a call from Emi and it&nbsp;
is revealed that she deliberately left the diary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:59.920
on his table. She promises to tell him everything&nbsp;
and asks him to meet her tomorrow in his classroom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:05.840
at 6 am. She also asks him to bring the mysterious&nbsp;
box with him. Just as the clock strikes 12&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:11.040
and before Takatoshi could get a word in, Emi&nbsp;
disappears from the phone booth like a ghost.
&nbsp;

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:16.400
The next day, Emi meets him in the classroom and&nbsp;
tells him that she is from a parallel world where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:22.000
time moves in the opposite direction. In other&nbsp;
words, what's the future for Takatoshi is the past&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:27.600
for Emi and vice versa. This explains how Emi knew&nbsp;
that Takatoshi’s picture was going to be displayed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:32.560
in his school. Takatoshi is left stunned by the&nbsp;
revelation and doesn’t believe any of it at first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:37.280
but when Emi tells her how she knew of his&nbsp;
mother’s secret recipe without ever meeting her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:40.320
he starts trusting her.
Emi then opens the box that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:45.760
the woman who saved Takatoshi from drowning gave&nbsp;
to him. Takatoshi is shocked to see a picture of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:52.640
Emi with his parents and him. She explains that&nbsp;
the picture is from her past i.e. his future. Emi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:57.760
has been watching Takatoshi from afar since he&nbsp;
was young and she was the adult woman who saved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:02.880
him and gave him the box. It is also revealed&nbsp;
that Takatoshi will save her from dying when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:08.720
she will be 5. Because her memories of him fade&nbsp;
as time goes on and her time goes backwards,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:13.600
she keeps a journal to remind her of him. She&nbsp;
also tells him that they can only be together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:18.880
for a month every five years because that’s&nbsp;
when Emi’s universe and Tatakoshi’s universe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:25.600
synchronizes. Moreover, 20 is the only time their&nbsp;
age matches and the current month is the last time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:30.080
where they can pursue a relationship. 
Despite them fast drifting apart,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:34.880
Emi tries to enjoy the moment but Takatoshi&nbsp;
feels conflicted about the fake nature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:39.440
of his and Emi's relationship. He tells her that&nbsp;
he can’t continue like this, saying he doesn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:43.840
want to enact a script from someone’s diary.&nbsp;
He meets his friend at the laundry shop and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:48.640
without revealing any details, he tells him&nbsp;
that Emi and he are moving past each other.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:53.920
Takatoshi compares Emi and himself to the earth&nbsp;
and moon that’s drifting away 4 centimetres from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:59.120
each other every year. However, Ueyama makes him&nbsp;
realize that it gives them all the more reason&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:03.920
to make the best of the time they have left&nbsp;
together. Suddenly, Takatoshi comprehends the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:09.440
reason why Emi used to get emotional all the time.&nbsp;
Takatoshi’s first meeting with Emi on the train&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:14.880
is actually Emi’s last, but Emi still acts as&nbsp;
if she has met Takatoshi for the first time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:20.400
Realizing this, Takatoshi becomes devastated&nbsp;
as Emi has been sacrificing her feelings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:26.000
just to stay relevant with the timeline. He then&nbsp;
immediately calls her and apologizes to her. From&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:30.400
that day on the two spend their remaining days&nbsp;
together cherishing every moment together. 
&nbsp;

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:36.960
On March 15, Takatoshi takes Emi to his hometown.&nbsp;
He shows her his favourite restaurant. Emi loves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:41.840
the food and stomps her foot on the ground like&nbsp;
a child in excitement. In a flashback scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:46.080
Takatoshi tells Emi that he only plays&nbsp;
football because his dad loves to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:50.480
him playing it. He tells her that when he&nbsp;
grows up, he wants to be a comic artist. 
&nbsp;

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:55.360
Back to the present, the lovebirds go to meet&nbsp;
Takatoshi’s parents. They are given a cold welcome&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.360 --> 00:09:00.480
by his father but his mother is elated to see&nbsp;
his girlfriend. Takatoshi’s mother makes dinner&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:05.760
for them and tells Emi about his childhood. When&nbsp;
Takatoshi’s father leaves after having dinner, his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:11.040
mother tells Emi that he only acts cold in front&nbsp;
of others but deep down he cares a lot about his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:16.400
son. The couple then takes the same family picture&nbsp;
from the box before leaving. On their way back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:21.680
Takatoshi breaks into tears, despairing over&nbsp;
the family he won’t get to start with Emi. 
&nbsp;

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:27.440
March 16 finally arrives. It is the last day&nbsp;
they would be together as equals. This is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:33.840
last day for Tatakoshi while it is the first day&nbsp;
for Emi. This Emi doesn’t remember how Tatakoshi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:39.520
and her spent the previous 30 days together as&nbsp;
every midnight, a new Emi meets Tatakoshi.
&nbsp;

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:44.240
They meet at Tatakoshi’s class because he has&nbsp;
been meaning to draw her since he first saw her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:48.880
Emi has a diary in which she has written how&nbsp;
she broadly spends her time with Tatakoshi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:54.480
according to what the 25 year old Tatakoshi told&nbsp;
her so she asks a 20 year old Tatakoshi to tell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:58.480
everything about their time together&nbsp;
in the last 30 days in as much detail&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.480 --> 00:10:03.120
as possible. She asks him this as from
now on, she intends to use this updated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:07.360
diary to relive their time together.&nbsp;
Takatoshi then delightfully explains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:12.400
to her about the blissful days while&nbsp;
drawing her. This brings him to tears. 
&nbsp;

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:18.480
Later, Takatoshi stays with Emi till midnight.&nbsp;
A few moments before midnight, Emi asks him what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:23.840
kind of girlfriend she was and if he was happy&nbsp;
with her. Tatakoshi tells her that the last 30&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:29.520
days with her were the best period of his life. He&nbsp;
also tells her that they are not drifting apart.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:35.680
The edges have been tied into a ring connecting&nbsp;
them as one life. The clock finally strikes 12 and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:41.840
Emi disappears. This makes Tatakoshi annoyed&nbsp;
but once he grasps reality, he calms down.
&nbsp;

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:48.240
Five years pass by. Tatakoshi is now 25. He meets&nbsp;
a 15 year old Emi and shows her the painting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:53.760
he drew of her 5 years ago. Emi notes how the&nbsp;
future Tatakoshi is more mature and wonderful. 
&nbsp;

00:10:57.840 --> 00:11:03.120
A further ten years later, Takatoshi rescues&nbsp;
5-year-old Emi from a festival fire. The film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:08.720
then cuts to a montage of the film presented from&nbsp;
Emi's perspective, in backwards, ending with her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.720 --> 00:11:15.040
and Takatoshi's introduction on February 15 on&nbsp;
the train, her last day she met him as equals
&nbsp;

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:17.760
